This is the release candidate of what will be the next major version of Nitrocid, which brings lots of general improvements and bug fixes, while introducing new features that are promising. User experience has been improved, and some long standing bugs have been fixed.

Nitrocid 0.2.1 will be released on November 5th, and all remaining bugs that have been found since the release candidate will be fixed in the final release, as well as a final set of improvements.

### Changes

This release contains a variety of changes, including, but not limited to:

- `[+]` Added user and group management TUI
- `[+]` Restored POP mail
- `[+]` Added search function for config and The Nitrocid Homepage
- `[+]` Added UNIX permission function
- `[+]` Added privileged method, field, and property attribute for inter-addon and inter-mod communication
- `[+]` Added screensavers and splashes
- `[*]` Updated Terminaux to v8.8
- `[*]` Updated native libraries
- `[*]` Improved calendar rendering
- `[*]` Improved the kernel codebase
- `[*]` General improvements and bug fixes
- `[-]` Removed kernel tips
- `[-]` Removed legacy theme studio

Review the commit history if you want to get a deep insight about the changes.

### Feedback?

If you have issues with this version, report to us by [making a new issue ticket](https://github.com/Aptivi/Nitrocid/issues/new).

